All three functions are implemented and `python3 test_impl.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (the stress loop took 6.2s). I ran the suite after each function, and `test_impl.py` is untouched.

- **`encode`** in `rle.py`: groups consecutive characters and writes each one followed by its run length.
- **`decode`** in `rle.py`: reads each non-digit character with the digits after it and expands it.
- **`merge`** in `intervals.py`: sorts by start and folds in any interval that starts at or before the current end, so touching intervals merge. It returns new lists and does not modify the input.

One limitation of the format itself: a string that contains digits (e.g. `"a11"`) will not round-trip, because the encoded form can't distinguish a digit character from a count. The tests don't cover this.

Changes are uncommitted, and the run left an untracked `__pycache__/` directory.
